# Written here rather than lifted, because the lifter cannot read it: 6.1
# chooses between two compound variables by arithmetic on where they are,
# a comparison's answer shifted left five and added to the address of the
# first, and they are not thirty-two bytes apart in this machine. It does
# what 6.1's set_phrase_defaults does: copies the one or the other into a
# third, according to whether the field it is handed is a variable's value.

rule set_phrase_defaults takes 2
  instead
  local parm bytes 8
  variable target word 2016
  variable unequal word 2030
  variable equal word 2044
  call get_parm addr parm arg 1 -4
  call fence 0 sym eti_null
  set global half 2410 to global half 2128
  if global half 1478 is cell parm field
    call copyvar addr target addr equal
    match
  end
  call copyvar addr target addr unequal
  match
end
